--- !u!114 &1874386781
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1874386779}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1f3ef889599182844a2f5643151998e9, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  readingMechanicTutorial: {fileID: 0}
  storyText: {fileID: 2102374086}
  fullText: "Why Dogs Wag Their Tails\n\nOnce upon a time, in a certain pueblo, there
    lived a wealthy man who owned a faithful dog and a clever cat.\n\nThe rich man
    adored his only daughter, who was studying far away at a convent school in the
    bustling city miles from home.\n\nEvery week without fail, he sent the dog and
    the cat on a special mission: to deliver a small present to his beloved daughter.\n\nThe
    dog, though old and toothless, knew the roads like the back of his paw.\n\nThe
    cat, agile and sharp-witted, guarded the gifts with care.\n\nTogether, they were
    a perfect team\u2014the dog leading the way while the cat watched their backs.\n\nOne
    day, the rich man decided to send a precious ring to his daughter. He called
    the two animals close.\n\nTo the cat, he said softly, \u201CYou are clever and
    careful. Carry this magic ring to my daughter, but take really good care of it.\u201D\n\nThen
    he turned to the dog, \u201CYou will go with the cat to protect her. Don\u2019t
    get lost, and make sure no harm comes to the ring.\u201D\n\nBoth the animals
    promised their master that they would do their best. With hearts full of purpose,
    they set off.\n\nTheir journey soon brought them to a wide, deep river\u2014its
    waters rushing fiercely without a single bridge in sight.\n\nThey searched for
    a boat but found none. After a moment of hesitation, they decided to swim across.\n\nThe
    dog looked to the cat and said, \u201CGive me the magic ring. I am stronger and
    can guard it better.\u201D\n\nThe cat\u2019s eyes narrowed. \u201CNo, don\u2019t
    you remember what the master said? You must protect me, and I must carry the
    ring.\u201D\n\n\u201CBut you\u2019re not a strong swimmer,\u201D the dog argued.
    \u201CI am strong and can hold the ring safely.\u201D\n\nThe cat refused, but
    the dog grew insistent, threatening her until she handed over the precious ring,
    trembling with fear.\n\nWith the ring now in his mouth, the dog and cat plunged
    into the cold river. The current was fierce, pulling at their bodies with relentless
    force. \n\nFor nearly an hour, they battled the rushing waters, their bodies
    becoming really tired.\n\nJust as they neared the opposite shore, disaster struck.\n\nThe
    dog\u2019s jaw loosened, and the magic ring slipped from his grasp, sinking beneath
    the surface and vanishing to the bottom.\n\nThe cat gasped. \u201CNow we must
    return and tell our master what had happened.\u201D\n\nThe dog whimpered, \u201CI\u2019m
    so scared... I don\u2019t want to face him.\u201D\n\nThey began the journey home,
    tired and worried. But as they neared the rich man\u2019s house, the dog felt
    true fear.\n\nWithout looking back, he fled into the wilderness\u2014and was
    never seen again.\n\nWhen the master saw that the cat returned alone, he frowned.
    \u201CWhere is the dog?\u201D he asked.\n\nThe cat\u2019s voice shook. \u201CHe...
    he ran away.\u201D\n\n\u201CRan away?\u201D the master repeated in confusion.
    \u201CAnd the ring? What happened to the ring?\u201D\n\nThe cat bowed her head.
    \n\n\u201CPlease forgive me, master. When we reached the river, the dog demanded
    the ring. I refused, but he threatened to kill me if I didn\u2019t obey. I had
    no choice.\u201D\n\n\u201CThe river was dangerous, and the dog dropped the ring.
    We could not find it. I convinced him to come back and tell you, but he was too
    afraid and ran away.\u201D\n\nAngered and disappointed, the master announced
    a reward for anyone who could find his old, toothless dog. \n\nBut here\u2019s
    the catch: he vowed to punish the dog by cutting off its tail. \n\nHe called
    upon all the dogs far and wide to help with the search.\n\nSince that day, when
    one dog meets another, it asks in hushed tones: \u201CAre you the old dog who
    lost the magic ring? If so, your tail must be cut off!\u201D\n\nImmediately,
    both dogs bare their teeth and wag their tails, signaling, \u201CNo, it is not
    me.\u201D\n\nAnd from that moment onwards, cats have held a deep fear of water.
    They will never swim across a river unless absolutely necessary.\n\n\u2013 THE
    END \u2013\n"
  scrollbar: {fileID: 510453668}
  lineSelector: {fileID: 510453667}
